  ;; --- compositional pairs, second batch (2026-09-19) --------------------
  ;;
  ;; P1 held out only ten compositional examples, and the noise control showed
  ;; why that is not enough: on pure noise one configuration scored 0.900 on
  ;; that subset.  At n=10 a single example is ten points.  These 56 pairs
  ;; bring the compositional half to 72 pairs, so a third of them held out is
  ;; 48 examples -- enough that 0.70 excludes chance rather than shrugging.
  ;;
  ;; Same construction rule as the first batch: the polarity-bearing words are
  ;; the SAME on both sides and the composition decides the sign.  "failed to
  ;; miss" against "failed to hit", "never conceded" against "never scored",
  ;; "missed the storm" against "missed the deadline".
  (:pair  71 :label 1 :hard t :text "She failed to miss the target.")
  (:pair  71 :label 0 :hard t :text "She failed to hit the target.")
